## Hints

- E1: if the outside-band fraction is 10–20%+, the constant-μ story is
  in trouble *for this sample* — but remember the SE assumes
  independence; vol clustering widens the TRUE band (n_eff < n), so
  the honest conclusion is "consistent with noise once dependence is
  priced in, and unprovable either way at this n."
- E3: mean shift: n = (2σ/Δ)²·2 (two SEs of difference, two samples);
  vol doubling: need 1/√(2n) small relative to the gap — solve.
